hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15528","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Abdullah, meaning Ibn Mubarak, informed us, he said: al-Awzai informed us, he said: al-Muttalib ibn Hantab al-Makhzumi narrated to me, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Amrah al-Ansari narrated to me, my father narrated to me, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in an expedition, and hunger afflicted the people, so the people sought permission from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to slaughter some of their mounts, and they said: Allah will carry us by it. So when Umar ibn al-Khattab saw that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was about to permit them to slaughter some of their mounts, he said: O Messenger of Allah, how will we be when we meet the enemy tomorrow, hungry, on foot? But if you see fit, O Messenger of Allah, to call for the remnants of their provisions and gather them, then supplicate Allah in them for blessing, for Allah the Blessed and Exalted will carry us by your supplication, or he said: will bless us in your supplication. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for the remnants of their provisions, and the people began bringing a handful of food and above that, and the highest of them was one who brought a sa of dates. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gathered them, then stood and supplicated as much as Allah willed to supplicate, then called the army with their vessels and ordered them to scoop up. So no vessel remained in the army but they filled it, and like it remained. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed until his molars appeared, and said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah, no believing servant meets Allah with them but he is veiled from the Fire on the Day of Resurrection."
